  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\frac{\\cos A}{\\cos B}=n, \\frac{\\sin A}{\\sin B}=m$, then the value of $\\left(m^{2}-n^{2}\\right) \\sin ^{2} B$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gZ5gT",
      "text": "$1+\\mathrm{n}^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "rWbmR",
      "text": "$1-\\mathrm{n}^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gH7NL",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{n}^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8HVZ1",
      "text": "$-\\mathrm{n}^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\cos A=n \\cos B$ and $\\sin A=m \\sin B$\r\n\r\nSquaring and adding, we get $1=n^{2} \\cos ^{2} B+m^{2} \\sin ^{2} B$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{array}{ll}\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow & 1=n^{2}\\left(1-\\sin ^{2} B\\right)+m^{2} \\sin ^{2} B \\\\\r\n\r\n\\therefore & \\left(m^{2}-n^{2}\\right) \\sin ^{2} B=1-n^{2}\r\n\r\n\\end{array}\r\n\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
